{{also|Brose}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the [[Doric]] dialect of North East Scotland, from earlier [[browes]], from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|broez|lang=fro}}, nominative of {{term|broet||stew, soup made from meat broth|lang=fro}} (French {{term|brouet|lang=fr}}) diminutive of {{term|breu|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|brodium|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|bruþą||broth|lang=gem-pro}}. See [[broth]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|Scotland}} [[oatmeal|Oatmeal]] mixed with [[boiling]] [[water]].

====Derived terms====
* [[brosy]], [[brosey]]
* [[brosy-faced]]

